    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1106">

                <pb facs="1596" n="1580" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1580"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.00/2–349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Legation in Saudi Arabia
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-19T13:00:00-05:00">February 19,
                            1949—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>62. Legtel 88 Feb. 3. You may inform FonMin in response his approach re Greater Syria
                    problem that although we are of course aware various ideas advanced in this
                    respect we have read no indications of any impending move toward realization. As
                        FonMin mentions annexation Arab part
                    Palestine to TJ would be first step you shld tell
                    him we <pb facs="1597" n="1581" xml:id="pg1581"/> wld not consider merger this
                    territory as recommended by UN Mediator to be related Greater Syria.</p>
                <p>You may wish add that mutuality US and UK interests is such that US wld not
                    hesitate approach Brit Govt again concerning Greater Syria problem if threat
                    affecting peace and security of ME shld
                    materialize. (Legtel 100 Feb 9.)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1106-f1"/> In your discretion you may remind SAG however that preservation peaceful cooperation
                    among Arab States is fundamentally and primarily responsibility of Arab
                    statesmen themselves.</p>
                <p>Re question arms embargo you may say we propose to give consideration to lifting
                    embargo when peace is restored in Palestine.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
